  of the most severe possible accusations  um the report specifically mentions  forced labor in those  political re-education camps and it also  mentions torture physical torture and it  refers also to the very drastically  plunging birth rates in some of the  counties in xinjiang and  experts and researchers have attributed  that to four sterilizations however what  the um report did not do it did not  answer the question whether what  happened in xinjiang constitutes a  genocide or cultural genocide or not it  doesn't really mention that question  based on the fact  of what you mentioned about  this evidence from  official documentation  what would you say about  the  reaction of beijing's  yeah so in the first reaction basically  beijing denied um everything it doesn't  really um deal with the criticism it  only says that this u.n report is uh is  stunned by a western governments and  what will happen probably is um that the  government here will  ramp up  censorship i don't think that the  criticism will find its way into the  chinese public discourse and also  probably xi jinping the state leader  will um  ramp up the nationalism here because in  six weeks there's a historic party  congress during which he will most  likely proclaim a third term in office  and during that time um yeah  stability is key for the leadership here  and they don't want to deal with any  criticism or  anything that could cause instability in  their eyes so i think the nationalism  will only get worse in the coming weeks  and um probably let me just briefly add  that sure and they will establish the  ratif that um  yeah they will establish the narrative  that basically the west is trying to um  limit china's rise and they will  basically victimize themselves and don't  want to deal with any criticism okay  fabian krejcimer in beijing thank you  very much for the insight  you
 

